*/Cloud Futures: Hot Topics in Research and Education/*

Berkeley, CA | May 7-8, 2012

http://research.microsoft.com/cloudfutures2012/

The Cloud Futures Workshop series brings together thought leaders from=20
academia, industry, and government to discuss the role of cloud=20
computing across a variety of research and educational areas---including=20
computer science, engineering, Earth sciences, healthcare, humanities,=20
interactive games, life sciences, and social sciences.Presentations,=20
posters and discussions will highlight how new techniques, software=20
platforms, and methods of research and teaching in the cloud may solve=20
distinct challenges arising in those diverse areas.

This year's Workshop is being hosted in conjunction with UC Berkeley.

Conference Co-Chairs: Michael Franklin, UC Berkeley and Tony Hey,=20
Microsoft Research

*Register today!=20
<https://www.ustechsregister.com/cloudfutures/default.aspx?pageid=3D3232>=
*

